      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَكْرَانُ مُلْتَخٌّ</span></b> , (S, K,) vulg. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُلْطَخٌّ</span>, (S,) or
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُلَطَّخٌ</span>, (as in some copies of the S and K,) but this
should not be said, (K,) <i>A drunken man confused
in his intellect,</i> (S, L,) <i>and not understanding
anything:</i> (L:) or, <i>full of drink;</i> (K;) as also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْتَخٌّ</span>. (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رخ</span>.) ― 
